This is sort of an essential "player-level" conflict
in this newsgroup.

To someone for whom getting to the endgame is a
regular occurance because slip-sliding through the
early and mid-game has become routine, of _course_
all of the game's resources should be preserved to
contribute to the ascension run.

To someone for whom getting to the mid-game is
nearly impossibly difficult, of _course_ every
resource should be employed to prolong the PC's
attempts to live long and prosper into the mid-game.

Both viewpoints are absolutely correct, they just
happen to be in violent disagreement.

Moral: It is much more useful to give advice
appropriate to the player-level experience of the
advice-recipient, not advice appropriate to the
player-level experience of the advice-giver.

